{
 "id": "20260926-223000-interaction-supervisor-relay-zero-copy-relay",
 "axis": "interaction",
 "hypothesis": "The supervisor-routed response relay's four-phase JSON re-materialization (from_slice parse + from_value per-key-clone walk + response_line deep clone + client-line to_string, ~28-40ms at 4.3-9.5MB wire per the decomposition record 20260926-193000) is removable: routing needs only the frame header's requestId plus the attach-family bookkeeping scalars, and the worker's own response_line bytes with the client id spliced in front are byte-identical to what the typed path emits (splice oracle proven on the same fixtures).",
 "approach": "CANDIDATE: zero-copy routed response relay. WorkerReply::Relayed carries the worker's response payload BYTES + ok/activeSessionId hints from the response frame's routing header (worker emits them for the attach family); the supervisor reader pump hands them to the route unparsed; route_client_command splices the client command id ('{\"id\":\"<cid>\",' + payload[1:]) and the connection writer emits raw bytes; attach-family bookkeeping runs from the header hints; the client-capabilities echo moves to the worker (routed attach request carries clientCapabilities; direct path unchanged). Typed path retained for chunked-snapshot attach clients, rebound reattach (command echo rewrite), detach/kill/rename/promote-owned forms, and every supervisor-internal route (route_command_typed parses back). Gate arms: detach, kill, rename, cron_add/heartbeat_set with promote_owned_session \u2014 verified by grep of every outcome-inspecting caller.",
 "parity_notes": "INTERNAL worker-socket protocol change (disclosed for reviewer ruling): the private-frame response HEADER gains optional ok/activeSessionId for attach-family responses, and the routed attach request payload gains an optional clientCapabilities array. Both sides in-tree; direct-attach clients parse the header as a JSON object and ignore unknown fields; the direct attach request carries no clientCapabilities and is byte-unchanged (parity-proven). The CLIENT-facing daemon socket is byte-identical per routed kind.",
 "wire_parity_per_routed_kind": {
  "method": "raw client-line dumps base vs candidate on the same fixtures; leaf-diff analysis of the differing payloads (attach-path's wire_parity.py method); A/A control (base vs base, fresh daemons) for the run-identity leaf set",
  "canon_10mib": {
   "get_messages_9474073B": "BYTE_IDENTICAL",
   "get_session_header": "BYTE_IDENTICAL",
   "detach": "BYTE_IDENTICAL",
   "splice_oracle_candidate": "routed get_messages line == '{\"id\":\"gm0\",' + worker payload[1:] BYTE_IDENTICAL",
   "attach_and_get_state": "identical modulo run-identity leaves; the candidate's 16 (attach, 80,461 leaves) / 6 (state, 40 leaves) diff leaves are EXACTLY the A/A control's leaf set (activeSessionId, client id, event-cursor generation uuids, worker instance/pid, session file path, modified timestamp) - no other leaf differs",
   "direct_attach_payload": "identical modulo the same identity-leaf set (one fewer: the direct client id is constant)"
  },
  "evidence": "/home/ubuntu/hillclimb/lane-supervisor-relay/canon-parity + aa-parity (raw dumps + leaf analysis)"
 },
